201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 606 0 R
/ActualText (React Testing Library \(RTL\) is a popular testing utility that is built on top of DOM Testing Library. It is designed specifically for testing React components in a way that closely mimics how users interact with your application.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
202 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 607 0 R
/ActualText (RTL focuses on testing components' behavior and interactions rather than their internal implementation details. This makes tests more reliable, less prone to breakage, and easier to maintain.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 608 0 R
/ActualText (It provides simple utilities to interact with DOM elements, making it easy to write readable tests.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
